@startuml AD_Image_Upload_Workflow
!theme cerulean-outline
title Product Image Upload Workflow
footer AdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

|#e8f0fe|Admin (Browser)|
|#e8f4e8|React Frontend|
|#fff3e0|ASP.NET Core Backend|
|#fce4ec|File System / Database|

|Admin (Browser)|
start
:Navigate to **Admin Dashboard**;

:Select **Products** tab;

|React Frontend|
:Load all products via\nGET /api/products;

:Render product list with\nimage upload controls;

|Admin (Browser)|
:Click **upload image** button\nfor a specific product;

:Select image file from\nlocal file system;

|React Frontend|
:Create **FormData** object\nwith IFormFile (multipart/form-data);

:POST /api/products/{id}/image\nContent-Type: multipart/form-data\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>;

|ASP.NET Core Backend|
:ProductsController.UploadImage()\nreceives id and IFormFile;

if (file is null or empty?) then (yes)
  :Return **400 BadRequest**\n"File is required.";
  |React Frontend|
  :Show error message;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Fetch product by ID\nfrom repository;

if (Product not found?) then (yes)
  :Return **404 NotFound**;
  |React Frontend|
  :Show error message;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Read Images:ProductsPath\nfrom configuration\n(default: C:\\images\\product);

:Ensure directory exists\n(Directory.CreateDirectory);

if (Product has existing\nImageFileName?) then (yes)
  :Build old file path\nand delete old image file\nfrom disk (if exists);
else (no)
endif

:Extract file extension\n(e.g. .png, .jpg);

:Validate file extension;

if (Extension in\n{.png, .jpg, .jpeg, .gif}?) then (no)
  :Return **400 BadRequest**\n"Invalid file type.";
  |React Frontend|
  :Show "Invalid file type" error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Generate unique filename:\n**product-{id}-{GUID}{ext}**\n(e.g. product-42-a1b2c3d4.png);

:Build full path:\nC:\\images\\product\\{filename};

|File System / Database|
:Create file on disk\nand copy uploaded stream\n(file.CopyToAsync);

:Update product.ImageFileName\n= generated filename;

:repo.UpdateAsync(product)\npersists to database;

|ASP.NET Core Backend|
:Fetch updated product;

:Return **200 OK**\nwith updated ProductDto\n(includes new ImageFileName);

|React Frontend|
:Receive updated ProductDto;

:Refresh product image via\nstatic file serving:\n**/images/product/{filename}**;

note right
  Static file middleware
  serves images from
  C:\images\product\
  mapped to /images/product/
end note

|Admin (Browser)|
:New product image\ndisplayed in the UI;

stop
@enduml
